{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789828251,"nonce":"N8MJa7+QauPE2dK7KaoefDKZ++U=","title":"OSR layout computation is quadratic in the region; 15 to 22 ms per large function at every start","message":"`osr_layout_with` cost 15 ms for `optparse$OptionParser$parse_args`\n(204 blocks, 3 headers), 16 ms for nbody's `advance`, 22 ms for\nnqueens' `__main__` (14 headers), measured on the NUC (x86_64) with\n`ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY=1` (`[clif] osr prologue`). Every speed-center kernel\npays the parse_args one because they all go through the optparse shim.\n\nTwo superlinear parts:\n\n- `region_dominators` was the set-based iterative algorithm: one\n  `HashSet` of all region blocks per block, intersected per predecessor\n  per iteration, iterating in hash order until convergence.\n- The repair scan walked every instruction of every region block once\n  per value defined in a block the header does not dominate, and\n  recomputed the \"reaches around the header\" DFS per value although it\n  depends only on the defining block.\n\nFix: region dominance as immediate dominators over the region's reverse\npostorder (the same iteration `Dominators::compute` uses), one reader\nindex (value -\u003e reading blocks, value -\u003e phi predecessors) per layout,\nand the around-set computed once per defining block, lazily.\n\nAfter: parse_args 1.0 ms, nqueens `__main__` 3.1 ms; no prologue above\n1 ms on fannkuch, nbody, meteor. Compile phase on the NUC: fannkuch 94\n-\u003e 82 ms, meteor 207 -\u003e 185 ms, nqueens 237 -\u003e 216 ms.","files":null}]}